;; Same target and the same three wants as instance-4.edn; a different route.
;;
;; Candidate A (instance-4.edn) is registry-first: name the grain, make the
;; binding a record, give it one producer, then transfer a caller. Candidate B
;; is the route Rob actually took in instance 6: derive a read-only view of
;; role-to-seat from what already exists, put routing through it behind an
;; explicit switch, make that the single authority, and only then convert and
;; retire. Neither is the mission's recommendation -- the mission names the
;; exit, not the order -- so both are honest readings of it.
;;
;; The contrast is the point. A branches at the root and its frontier is wide;
;; B is nearly a chain, where clause 0 says a precedence list is the chain case
;; of the containment order and all three kernels must agree.
;; Authored by claude-1, 2026-09-24. DRAFT pending claude-10's review.
